 argument has to be the same thing the parameter declares. Handing a stamp
 to a function expecting a point would copy sixteen bytes of postage into
 sixteen bytes of coordinates, which the caller cannot see going wrong.

 The second call passes a number, which has no whole shape to copy at all.)

